<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Group Five raises full yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>Group Five raises full yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 1996.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     83.8	  vs     62.3</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 20.0	  vs     14.0</p>
<p>    Attrib profit	   35.03	 vs     26.03</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   52.99	 vs     66.81</p>
<p>    Tax			 16.25	 vs     16.22</p>
<p>    Turnover	     2,494.83	 vs  2,249.06</p>
<p>Div payable: October 11</p>
<p>On register: September 27</p>
<p>Full name: Group Five Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group's core divisions -- building and property development and roads and earthworks -- contributed the bulk of the group's profits.</p>
<p>Excluding Everite Holdings Ltd, the construction group's taxed profit jumped 82 percent on a 20 percent rise in turnover, well above the current trend in South Africa's construction industry, which was hurt by an expected take off in social housing that started slowly and low fixed investment growth.</p>
<p>The group said it was financially stronger than ever before with very little borrowing.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
